# VS Code REST Client requests against the running mock (task mocks:up && task mocks:load)
@base = http://localhost:8585/rest/Pizza+Service+API/1.0.0

### Make a pizza (202)
POST {{base}}/commands/make-pizza
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa

{ "size": "medium", "crust": "sourdough", "toppings": ["mozzarella", "basil"] }

### Invalid command (400)
POST {{base}}/commands/make-pizza
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa

{ "size": "banana", "crust": "sourdough", "toppings": [] }

### Status: accepted — what the statusUrl returns right after a 202
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### Status: topped
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112

### Status: cooked
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111113

### Status: boxed
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111114

### Status: ready
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111115

### Status: failed
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111116

### Status: cancelled
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111117

### Unknown pizza (404)
GET {{base}}/pizzas/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

### Slow response — override mock latency for timeout testing
GET {{base}}/pizzas/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111?delay=2000

### Cancel a pizza (202)
POST {{base}}/commands/cancel-pizza
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb

{ "pizzaId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "reason": "Changed my mind" }

### Cancel a terminal pizza (409)
POST {{base}}/commands/cancel-pizza
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb

{ "pizzaId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111115", "reason": "Too late" }
